with nq as (
  insert into public.questions (stage, question_type, stem, model_answer, explanation, key_points, subject_id, topic_id, paper_id, difficulty, marks,
                                estimated_seconds, origin, status, parent_question_id, variation_type, ai_review, passage_group, passage_position, verified_by, subject_group_id, specialisation_id, image_url)
  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'Prime Minister Tshering Tobgay recently issued an executive order mandating that all government meetings and official correspondence be conducted in Dzongkha. Although similar orders to promote and use Dzongkha have been issued many times in the past, the Bhutanese preference for English has persisted, making the implementation of these policies challenging. Discuss some of the significant challenges faced and what, in your opinion, needs to be done to overcome them. (20 marks)', 'Dzongkha is the national language under Article 1 of the Constitution and a pillar of national identity, unity and sovereignty. The Prime Minister''s executive order aims to make it the working language of government, but past efforts show real obstacles.
Challenges:
1. Education: English is the medium of instruction for most subjects from school to university, so most educated Bhutanese think, read and write more comfortably in English; many write Dzongkha poorly.
2. Vocabulary: Dzongkha lacks standard technical terms for many modern fields (finance, ICT, law, science, medicine), so drafting technical documents is slow and difficult.
3. Technology: limited Dzongkha software, spell-checkers, keyboards and digital content; older legacy fonts cause compatibility problems.
4. Attitudes: English is associated with prestige, modernity and job opportunities, while Dzongkha is sometimes seen as only for formal or religious use.
5. International work: donors, international agreements and many reports require English.
6. Diversity: Bhutan has many mother tongues (Tshangla, Lhotshamkha and others), so Dzongkha is a second language for many.
7. Weak enforcement: past orders were not monitored, and there were no consequences or incentives.
What needs to be done:
1. Strengthen Dzongkha teaching at all levels, with better methods, materials and teachers, and make it more relevant to everyday and professional use.
2. Dzongkha Development Commission to develop and publish technical terminology, glossaries, templates and translation services for government documents.
3. Invest in digital tools - Unicode fonts, keyboards, spell-checkers, machine translation and Dzongkha content online and in media.
4. Train civil servants in Dzongkha writing and make proficiency part of recruitment, training and performance evaluation.
5. Leaders and senior officials should lead by example in meetings and correspondence.
6. Implement in phases with monitoring, while allowing English where necessary for technical and international matters.
7. Promote pride in Dzongkha through literature, films, music and competitions.
With patient, practical implementation, Dzongkha can become a living working language without losing the benefits of English.', null, '[{"point": "Importance of Dzongkha: national language (Article 1), identity, sovereignty, culture, unity", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Challenges: English as medium of instruction and of higher education/ ICT/ business; limited Dzongkha technical vocabulary and terminology; weak Dzongkha writing skills among officials; lack of Dzongkha software/ keyboards/ fonts and digital content; attitude - English seen as prestigious/ global; international partners and documents in English; multilingual society; weak enforcement and monitoring", "marks": 9}, {"point": "Solutions: strengthen Dzongkha in education at all levels; develop terminology, dictionaries, translation and standard fonts/ tools (DDC); training for civil servants; incentives and performance indicators; leaders as role models; Dzongkha digital/ media content; enforce with monitoring but practical flexibility for technical/ international work", "marks": 8}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'language-and-national-identity'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 20,
    2160, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
