  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) The role of modern media is extremely crucial for strengthening the democratic process by educating citizens on relevant issues. The media is expected to perform four basic functions: provider of information, interpreter of events, initiator of public debate, and watchdog for the people. Discuss how, in your opinion, the Bhutanese media is performing these functions in making Bhutan''s democracy vibrant and sustaining. (10 marks)', 'a) Information: BBS, Kuensel and private newspapers, radio and online news inform citizens about government decisions, parliamentary debates, elections and development, reaching rural areas in Dzongkha and English. Interpretation: editorials, analysis and expert discussions help citizens understand policies such as tourism reform, civil service reform and the economy. Public debate: talk shows, election debates (including the ECB-organised debates), letters and social media give people space to discuss issues. Watchdog: newspapers have exposed corruption, misuse of public funds and poor service delivery, leading to ACC investigations and reforms.
However, performance is limited: private media struggle financially in a small market and depend on government advertising, which can lead to self-censorship; journalists have limited capacity and resources for investigative work; and social media spreads misinformation. Supporting media independence, sustainable funding, training and media literacy will make democracy more vibrant.', null, '[{"point": "Assessment of each function with Bhutanese examples: information (BBS, Kuensel, private papers, online news, parliament coverage); interpreter (editorials, analysis); public debate (talk shows, social media, election debates); watchdog (investigative reporting on corruption, ACC cases)", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Limitations: financial viability of private media, small market, government advertising dependence, self-censorship, capacity, social media misinformation; suggestions", "marks": 4}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'democracy-media-and-the-constitution'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
