with nq as (
  insert into public.questions (stage, question_type, stem, model_answer, explanation, key_points, subject_id, topic_id, paper_id, difficulty, marks,
                                estimated_seconds, origin, status, parent_question_id, variation_type, ai_review, passage_group, passage_position, verified_by, subject_group_id, specialisation_id, image_url)
  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) Article 2, Clause 2 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Bhutan states: "The Chhoe-sid-nyi of Bhutan shall be unified in the person of the Druk Gyalpo who, as a Buddhist, shall be the upholder of the Chhoe-sid." In your opinion, what could be the possible rationale behind this clause? Explain. (10 marks)', 'b) Possible rationale: (1) Continuity - since Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel, Bhutan has been governed under the dual system (chhoe-sid nyi) of spiritual and temporal authority; the clause preserves this foundation in the constitutional monarchy. (2) Unity - the Druk Gyalpo is the symbol of the unity of the Kingdom and of its people; uniting the spiritual and the temporal in one person avoids rivalry between religious and secular power. (3) Identity and values - Buddhism is the spiritual heritage of Bhutan (Article 3) and shapes its culture, ethics and GNH, so the King as a Buddhist upholds these values. (4) Legitimacy and stability - the monarch commands respect from both the monastic body and the people, giving stability during the transition to democracy. (5) Balance - the King upholds both, while Article 3 keeps religious institutions above politics and protects freedom of religion for all citizens.', null, '[{"point": "Rationale: continuity of the dual system (chhoe-sid) established by Zhabdrung; King as unifying symbol; Buddhist heritage as foundation of identity and values; spiritual and temporal harmony", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Also: legitimacy and stability, balance and protection - King upholds both religion and state; Article 3 keeps religion separate from politics and protects all faiths; GNH values", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'democracy-media-and-the-constitution'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
