with nq as (
  insert into public.questions (stage, question_type, stem, model_answer, explanation, key_points, subject_id, topic_id, paper_id, difficulty, marks,
                                estimated_seconds, origin, status, parent_question_id, variation_type, ai_review, passage_group, passage_position, verified_by, subject_group_id, specialisation_id, image_url)
  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'Lama Jangchub Tsondru, root teacher of Jigme Namgyel, foretold, "The son born to Jigme Namgyel would establish hereditary rule in Bhutan." This prophecy came true when Jigme Namgyel''s son Ugyen Wangchuck became the First Hereditary Monarch of Bhutan. Discuss the events that led the people of Bhutan to choose and install Trongsa Penlop Ugyen Wangchuck as the First Hereditary Monarch of Bhutan. (20 marks)', 'Background: after Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel, Bhutan was governed under the dual system by the Je Khenpo and the Desi, but from the 18th century the central authority weakened. The Desis were often weak or short-lived, and the regional governors - especially the Penlops of Trongsa and Paro and the Dzongpons of Punakha, Wangdue and Thimphu - fought each other for power. Civil wars and instability lasted for much of the 19th century, and conflict with British India (the Duar War of 1864-65) led to the loss of the Duars. Jigme Namgyel, the Black Regent, rose as Trongsa Penlop and Desi and made Trongsa the strongest power.
Rise of Ugyen Wangchuck: his son Ugyen Wangchuck became Penlop of Trongsa. In 1885, at the Battle of Changlimithang in Thimphu, he defeated his rivals, ending the long period of civil war. He then established peace, order and unity across the country, ruled with wisdom and generosity, and supported religion, earning the trust of the clergy and the people.
External role: during the British expedition to Tibet led by Younghusband in 1903-04, he acted as mediator between the British and the Tibetans, winning respect and recognition; the British honoured him with a knighthood (KCIE) in 1905. His good relations with British India strengthened Bhutan''s security and sovereignty.
Installation: as the only leader able to keep the country united and secure, he was unanimously chosen as hereditary monarch by an assembly of the monastic body led by the Je Khenpo, the Penlops, Dzongpons, officials and representatives of the people, with Gongzim Ugyen Dorji playing an important role. On 17 December 1907 he was enthroned at Punakha Dzong as the First Druk Gyalpo, and a genja (written oath of allegiance) was signed, pledging loyalty to him and his heirs. This day is now celebrated as National Day.
Thus his leadership in ending civil war, unifying the country and protecting it externally fulfilled Lama Jangchub Tsondru''s prophecy and established the Wangchuck dynasty.', null, '[{"point": "Background: decline of the dual system after Zhabdrung - weak Desis, frequent civil wars and rivalry between Penlops and Dzongpons in the 18th-19th centuries; Jigme Namgyel (Trongsa Penlop, Desi) strengthened Trongsa", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Ugyen Wangchuck''s rise: Penlop of Trongsa; victory at Battle of Changlimithang (1885) ended civil war and consolidated power; restored peace and order, unified the country", "marks": 5}, {"point": "External relations: mediated between British India and Tibet during the Younghusband expedition (1903-04); British recognition (Knight Commander, KCIE 1905); good relations protected sovereignty", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Installation: people, clergy and officials, led by the Je Khenpo, Penlop of Paro, Dzongpons and representatives, unanimously chose him; Gongzim Ugyen Dorji''s role; enthroned at Punakha on 17 December 1907; genja (oath of allegiance) signed - now National Day", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Reasons: his leadership, piety, wisdom and ability to bring peace and unity; fulfilment of prophecy", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-the-monarchy'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 20,
    2160, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
