  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) He is known as the ''Divine Madman'' or the ''Maverick Saint'' for his unorthodox teaching of Buddhism. He is a ''culture hero'' around whom a web of stories, legends, facts and realities revolve. Discuss some of Choeje Drukpa Kunley''s contributions that shaped the richness of the religious, social and cultural life of the Bhutanese people. (10 marks)', 'a) Lam Drukpa Kunley (1455-1529), a master of the Drukpa Kagyu lineage, travelled from Tibet and spread Buddhism in Bhutan in an unconventional way. Religious: he taught the Dharma through humour, songs, poetry and shocking behaviour, making Buddhism accessible to ordinary people and exposing the hypocrisy of those who followed religion only outwardly. He is believed to have subdued demons and evil spirits - including the demoness of Dochula - and Chimi Lhakhang near Lobesa, built in his honour, is visited by couples seeking children and blessings. Social: by challenging rigid conventions and the pride of religious elites, he encouraged honesty, compassion and simplicity. Cultural: the painted and carved phallus symbols on houses and in fields, believed to ward off evil and bring fertility, come from his tradition; his legends - such as the creation of the takin - and his songs and stories are part of Bhutanese folklore, humour and festivals, and his descendants and lineage continue in Bhutan.', null, '[{"point": "Drukpa Kunley (1455-1529) of the Drukpa lineage: spread Buddhism among ordinary people through humour, songs and unconventional methods; subdued demons (Dochula, Chimi Lhakhang, Lobesa); Chimi Lhakhang as fertility temple", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Social and cultural contributions: challenged hypocrisy and rigid conventions, made Dharma accessible; phallus symbols for protection and fertility on houses; stories, legends, songs, festivals; takin legend; descendants and lineage", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-culture-and-citizenship'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (General): BCSE 2024, batch 2", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2024 Main Examination, General category, Paper III", "year": 2024, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/bcse-past-question-papers/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-general-3-2024b2-a4', 1, null, null, null, null)
