with nq as (
  insert into public.questions (stage, question_type, stem, model_answer, explanation, key_points, subject_id, topic_id, paper_id, difficulty, marks,
                                estimated_seconds, origin, status, parent_question_id, variation_type, ai_review, passage_group, passage_position, verified_by, subject_group_id, specialisation_id, image_url)
  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) His Majesty The King Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck said, "democracy is the renewed sense of duty and responsibility entrusted to the people to further strengthen the country..." In this context, explain some of the duties and responsibilities of Bhutanese citizens that you think would be most important in a democratic society to further strengthen the country. (10 marks)', 'b) Important duties and responsibilities of citizens in a democracy (many in Article 8 of the Constitution): (1) take part in elections and vote wisely and freely, after learning about candidates and policies; (2) preserve, protect and defend the sovereignty, security and unity of the country; (3) respect and uphold the Constitution and the rule of law; (4) foster tolerance, mutual respect and harmony among all people, rising above regional and party differences; (5) protect the environment, culture and heritage; (6) pay taxes and use public resources responsibly; (7) refuse corruption and report wrongdoing; (8) hold leaders accountable through informed participation, local government and responsible use of media; and (9) help others during disasters and national needs (e.g. Desuung). When citizens fulfil these duties, democracy becomes not only a system of rights but a shared responsibility that strengthens the nation, as His Majesty said.', null, '[{"point": "Duties (Article 8): vote and participate in elections, be informed, preserve sovereignty/ security/ unity, respect law and Constitution, pay taxes, protect environment and culture, tolerance and harmony, help in calamities, act against corruption", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Explains why each strengthens democracy; accountability of leaders, civic participation, responsible media use", "marks": 4}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-culture-and-citizenship'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
