  values ('ME', 'analytical', 'The 13th Five Year Plan (July 2024 to June 2029) has adopted a 10-year strategic framework to support the nation''s long-term goal of becoming a High Income GNH Economy by 2034 - driven by the interconnected pillars of people, progress and prosperity.

a) Define and explain the concept of a "High Income GNH Economy", providing relevant examples. (5 marks)', 'a) A High Income GNH Economy means an economy in which Bhutan reaches the income level of high-income countries - the plan aims for an economy of about USD 10 billion and per capita income at the high-income level by 2034 - but achieves this in line with Gross National Happiness: growth that is sustainable, inclusive and green, that preserves culture and the environment, and that improves wellbeing, not just income. Examples: growth through clean hydropower and solar energy, high-value low-volume tourism, digital and knowledge industries, organic agriculture and the Gelephu Mindfulness City as an economic hub - creating well-paid jobs for Bhutanese while keeping forest cover and cultural values.', null, '[{"point": "Definition: high income level (per capita income reaching World Bank high-income threshold, economy about USD 10 billion by 2034) achieved in a GNH way - sustainable, equitable, preserving culture and environment and wellbeing; examples (green/ digital industries, GMC, high value tourism, hydropower/ clean energy, quality jobs)", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
