  values ('ME', 'analytical', '"The recommendation of the National Assembly''s Economic and Finance Committee on the need to allocate Project Tied Assistance (PTA) and Small Development Project (SDP) resources to local governments using a Resource Allocation Formula has not been passed. Currently, this formula is used only for block grant allocation. During the National Assembly session held on 19 June 2024, 21 members supported the recommendation and 24 opposed it, making it ineffective."

a) What is your view on the necessity of allocating Project Tied Assistance (PTA) and Small Development Project (SDP) resources to local governments through a Resource Allocation Formula (RAF)? (10 marks)', 'a) A Resource Allocation Formula distributes resources to dzongkhags and gewogs using objective criteria such as population, area, poverty, transport cost and development needs. It is currently used for block grants, while Project Tied Assistance (donor- or project-linked funds) and Small Development Projects are allocated in other ways, often by the central government or through members'' and local proposals.
In my view, applying a formula-based approach - at least to SDP resources - is necessary because it would make allocation fairer, more transparent and predictable; reduce the risk of resources being directed by political influence or lobbying (a concern in a democracy, especially near elections); help local governments plan with known budgets; and reduce disparities between well-connected and remote gewogs. However, PTA funds are often tied to specific donor projects and conditions, so they may need some flexibility; a hybrid approach (formula for the bulk, with a needs-based portion) could balance both.', null, '[{"point": "Explains RAF (criteria such as population, area, poverty, transport cost index, development gaps) and current use for block grants; clear view with reasons - fairness, transparency, predictability, reduce political/ discretionary allocation, balanced regional development; or reasons for caution", "marks": 10}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'local-government-and-public-finance'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
